## Runtime adapter facts

Host: Cursor. If the running host is not Cursor, ignore this adapter section entirely and use the Kaola adapter installed for the actual host; if none is installed, record `capability_gap: no Kaola adapter for host <name>` and work inline.

Find custom profiles in project `.cursor/agents/` or user `~/.cursor/agents/`; a file on disk is not discovery proof, so inspect the live catalog. CLI, App local, and App Cloud are separate hosts. Materialize the selected project explicitly.
If the exact Kaola role is present and its materialized profile receipt is valid, call `Task` with the live flat `subagent_type: "<role>"` field and MUST omit the per-call `model`; an exact-binding requirement is a post-resolution assertion, never authorization to populate that field. In a built-in-only enum, omit-model is the parent, not a profile pin.

**Subagent default:** every installed Kaola profile pins `model: grok-4.7[effort=medium]`; a custom subagent that omits `model` inherits the parent, so the pin is what selects the cheaper child; omit the per-call `model`.
**Roles:** `code-explorer`, `code-reviewer`, `doc-updater`, `implementer`, `investigator`, `knowledge-lookup`, `tdd-guide`.

The named profile's native `readonly` flag carries its write boundary.
Inspect the live Task catalog. Measured hosts exposed writable `generalPurpose` and host-specific built-ins; some hosts document scoped `Explore`, `Bash`, or `Browser`. Use only a route this host reports, under its real identity and capability.
The live Task catalog is authoritative; CLI profile reload requires a new process.

If the exact name is absent, first distinguish an uninstalled or unsaved host carrier from a capability gap. Then inspect real alternatives for this item; a miss that the item's brief cannot absorb inlines only that item and records the specific `capability_gap`.
